From c1478816ec9eb699491da6a96c31306e4fc066cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dividebysandwich <josef.jahn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 15:17:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] hdr: apply connector color state via smithay's atomic
 commit

Replaces the standalone connector-property commits (max bpc via
ConnectorProperties, Colorspace + HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA via
apply_connector_hdr) with smithay's new ConnectorColorState API. The
render loop now only *stages* the desired color state; smithay applies
it inside its own frame submission as a single atomic modeset together
with mode, CRTC and plane state. Committing connector color properties
standalone is what hung the nvidia driver (it treats a Colorspace
change as a full modeset and wedges on incomplete pipeline state) --
confirmed also at 8-bit, so scanout depth was not the trigger.

Also:
- switch the wp-color-management-v1 implementation to smithay's
  wayland::color::management module (ported from ours, now with
  spec-correct double-buffered surface state and surface_exists/inert
  error handling)
- probe driver support (Colorspace BT2020_RGB, HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA,
  max bpc range) and the sink's EDID (PQ EOTF, BT.2020, desired
  luminances) at connector setup; warn when the config asks for HDR on
  an incapable output
- derive the HDR metadata infoframe from client mastering data clamped
  to the EDID, falling back to EDID desired-content values (fixes the
  500-nit placeholder TODO)
- clamp max bpc to the connector's supported range
- fall back to 8-bit scanout formats if creating the compositor with
  10-bit formats fails
- track driver-rejected color states so they are not re-tested every
  frame; retry after resume and config reload

Requires the local smithay branch hdr-for-niri (Cargo path patch).
